# The program and the deeds of a-change-of-a-class-that-a-proof-rules-out-ends-the-process.ir, built to admit the inspector. The console takes an instance out of the heap as the shell does here, and goes on to the prototype object and to the class object.
# The prototype object is an ordinary object: the run time hears of a change behind it. Where code that is not compiled made it, the change is taken back from the class record (the same function as before, the added name gone, the written link laid again) and a TypeError is thrown: the process goes on.
